vms-fd1: VMS host -- DELETE_IF_ORDINARY uses error ("%s: %m"), as gcc.cc does

gcc/config/vms/xm-vms.h overrides DELETE_IF_ORDINARY (the VMS form loops,
deleting every version of the file).  Its failure report still calls
perror_with_name, which gcc.cc no longer defines: the driver's own default
DELETE_IF_ORDINARY reports the same failure with error ("%s: %m", (NAME)).
A VMS-hosted build of gcc.cc therefore fails ("'perror_with_name' was not
declared in this scope").  Use the driver's current reporting call.

--- a/gcc/config/vms/xm-vms.h
+++ b/gcc/config/vms/xm-vms.h
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
       if (unlink (NAME) < 0)                               \
 	{                                                  \
 	  if (VERBOSE_FLAG)                                \
-	    perror_with_name (NAME);                       \
+	    error ("%s: %m", (NAME));                    \
 	  break;                                           \
 	}                                                  \
   } while (0)
